<!--
  ZeroAlloc.Rest v3.0.0: intentional API breaks for #336, splitting the Microsoft.Extensions DI and
  IHttpClientFactory dependency tree out of core.

  ServiceCollectionExtensions (AddZeroAllocClient, both AddRestSerializer overloads,
  DefaultClientName), ZeroAllocClientBuilder, ZeroAllocClientOptions, IGeneratedRestClient&lt;TSelf&gt;,
  RestSerializerServiceProviderExtensions, and GeneratedRestClient.Create/AddSerializers/
  AddPerClientSerializer all move to the new package ZeroAlloc.Rest.DependencyInjection, keeping the
  same ZeroAlloc.Rest namespace; the GeneratedRestClient members land on the new
  GeneratedRestClientRegistration type there. docs/migrating-to-v3.md maps every moved member to its
  new package.

  RestSerializerAdapter&lt;T&gt; is deleted outright, along with core's ZeroAlloc.Serialisation
  dependency.

  Generated by apicompat in suppression-file mode against the 2.2.0 baseline of each package, then
  annotated. The 2.0.0 CP0021 entry for AddRestResilience's TRestClient constraint was dropped: that
  constraint was already present in the 2.2.0 baseline, so it is unnecessary against it. Only the
  moved and removed types are listed, so an accidental removal elsewhere still fails the job.
-->
